Third-party material
--------------------

No code from another project is copied here. One acknowledgement is worth
making explicit: macho_grow.h says its approach was "studied from LIEF
(src/MachO/Binary.cpp `shift`) and llvm-objcopy (MachOLayoutBuilder)", and
that the exhaustive list of Mach-O file-offset fields was taken from LIEF.

That list is a factual enumeration of the file format rather than expression,
and the algorithm here is independent — LIEF and llvm-objcopy raise every later
segment to a higher vm address, whereas this lowers the image base so no vm
address changes at all. LIEF is Apache-2.0; llvm-objcopy is Apache-2.0 with
LLVM exceptions. Recorded so the acknowledgement in the source is not mistaken
for an undisclosed dependency.
